    "summary": "Fire‑filled second set with Dark Star, Not Fade Away and explosive drums",
    "blurb": "The late show erupts into a scorching electric marathon highlighted by an epic Dark Star and a 12‑minute drum odyssey that rolls straight into a monster Not Fade Away. Jerry’s soaring lead work and the twin‑drum explosion keep the energy high, while acoustic gems like Hard To Handle, Dark Hollow and Katie Mae shine in the earlier set.",
    "review": "On February 14, 1970 at the Fillmore East the Dead delivered a show that still feels fresh after more than five decades. The early acoustic half rolls through tight renditions of Casey Jones, Hard To Handle, Dark Hollow and the sweet duet of Katie Mae before launching into a blistering electric second set. Jerry Garcia’s lead work is described as “orbiting” and “arabesque,” his tone flawless on an extended Dark Star that segues into the post‑drums explosion. Bill Kreutzmann and Mickey Hart dominate the 12‑minute drum segment, building tension that bursts out into a marathon Not Fade Away, which stretches into a jam that never loses its momentum. Phil Lesh provides a solid, supportive foundation throughout, even getting front‑heavy praise on Hard To Handle. Highlights also include Uncle John’s Band, Black Peter, Caution (Do Not Stop On Tracks) and the seamless flow of the set’s segues. The crystal‑clear Miller soundboard capture (gd1970-02-14.sbd.miller.97644.flac16) presents this performance with excellent balance and “extra crispy” clarity, making it the definitive listening source despite a few missing early moments.",
